# .trivyignore — Trivy vulnerability ignore file
#
# Zero-tolerance policy: every entry here MUST include owner, reason, and expiry.
# Expired entries will be removed during periodic review.
#
# Format:
#   # owner: <name> | reason: <justification> | expires: YYYY-MM-DD
#   CVE-XXXX-XXXXX
#
# Example:
#   # owner: security-team | reason: not reachable in our stack | expires: 2026-06-01
#   CVE-2026-12345

# owner: security-team | reason: Google Spanner's metrics stack pins OpenTelemetry SDK 1.x; EnterpriseGlue does not configure OpenTelemetry baggage propagation, so the oversized HTTP baggage-header path is unreachable. Remove after the upstream Spanner dependency moves to SDK 2.x. | expires: 2026-11-01
CVE-2026-54285

# owner: security-team | reason: EnterpriseGlue is a client-side SPA and does not enable React Router RSC mode or server actions, so the RSC action CSRF path is absent. Remove after react-router-dom publishes a compatible React Router 8 release. | expires: 2026-11-01
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2

# owner: security-team | reason: The final backend libz bytes are rebuilt from the signed zlib 1.3.2 source with the complete stale-pointer remediation and regression test from madler/zlib#1286. Trivy sees the retained Chainguard APK metadata rather than the patched shared-library bytes. Remove when Chainguard publishes a fixed trusted zlib package. | expires: 2026-10-15
CVE-2026-85091
